WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.510
It’s the late 90's, and an Air Canada flight
experiences severe malfunctions while traveling

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.400
from London to Vancouver.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.330
The pilots are unable to do anything and the
plane crashes into the woods of Northern Alberta.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.800
The crash was devastating - only 10 of the
nearly 300 people on board are alive.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.660
And even though they survived the initial
disaster, their battle for life has only just

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.660
begun.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.550
It’s late autumn in Northern Canada and
there’s no telling when help will arrive,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.690
if at all.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:34.050
If the survivors want to make it through the
night they need to find shelter, and fast.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.699
As they trudge through the freezing woods,
the group finds a path that looks like it

00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:40.110
might lead them to civilization.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.539
After all, if there was a path in the woods,
that meant they were probably in a national

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:48.280
park, and if they were in a national park,
there had to be a ranger's station around

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.870
somewhere where they could warm up and call
for help.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.940
They didn’t have many other options, so
they followed the path which opened up to

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.539
a clearing, but instead of finding a ranger's
station or campground, they found something

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:01.280
none of them could have expected.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.860
It was a pond, but there was something off
about it.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.670
As they got closer they saw that this strange
pond wasn’t filled with water, but blood.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.159
The survivors were horrified.

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:14.610
That couldn't really be blood, could it?

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.540
It must be a weird algae or a chemical reaction.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.700
But one member of the group, a man named Thomas
Dean, who had been on his way back to his

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.600
hometown of Prince George, British Columbia,
thought there was something strangely familiar

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.600
about this.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.409
He remembered being a boy and going to visit
family in Alberta, and hearing an urban legend

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:34.210
from the older local kids.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.700
According to the stories, somewhere out in
the wilderness, in the northern part of the

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.420
province, there was a pond full of human blood,
and what made it even worse, was that some

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.979
said the pond was a gateway to hell.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:51.789
The SCP Foundation was also aware of this
legend, and had been trying to pinpoint the

00:01:51.789 --> 00:01:55.789
exact source of it for decades prior to the
Air Canada crash.

00:01:55.789 --> 00:02:00.259
They would finally receive definite confirmation
of the blood pond when Foundation personnel

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:05.649
intercepted a radio transmission from a ranger's
station located within the Wood Buffalo National

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:06.649
Park.

00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:10.720
It was the survivors of the crash, who had
managed to make it through the night, and

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.720
they were about to be escorted out of the
park by rangers.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.730
The Foundation mobilized quickly to cordon
off the pond, as at this time they were unsure

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.950
of what potentially harmful properties the
pond might have had.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:26.080
They set up Watch Station Epsilon-38 and put
staff on guard to deter travellers from the

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.080
area.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.100
The pond was given the designation of SCP-354
and classed as Euclid.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.959
Foundation scientists made a number of interesting
discoveries about SCP-354 when they collected

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:38.040
samples for testing.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:44.190
First, the pond was not in fact full of blood,
merely an inorganic liquid that closely resembles

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.200
blood in color and consistently.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.411
Second, and even stranger than the red liquid,
is that the pond doesn't seem to have definite

00:02:51.411 --> 00:02:52.890
banks or a bottom.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:57.480
Instead, the liquid in the pond increases
in density as the radius away from the center

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.819
increases - the liquid congeals at the edges,
becoming more solid and blending into the

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:03.880
surrounding soil.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.700
It also becomes thicker as one descends deeper
into the pool, and a bottom of the pond has

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.760
not yet been reached, if it even exists.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.299
Initially, the foundation found no signs of
life within the blood pond.

00:03:15.299 --> 00:03:20.930
But that would all change at 2:03 PM on the
day following the opening of Watch Station

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:25.689
Epsilon-38, when the science team noticed
an unusual level of activity on the pond's

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:26.689
surface.

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:30.769
Security footage feeds showed a shape rising
up out of the pond, followed by a deafening

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:31.769
shriek.

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:35.930
After that, the feed was cut and Foundation
lost all communication with Watch Station

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:36.930
Epsilon-38.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:40.650
Fearing the worst, a Mobile Task Force was
dispatched to the location.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.770
When they got there, all personnel at the
watch station had been killed by what could

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:47.510
only be described as a gigantic bat.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.200
The task force was able to neutralize the
entity, and as soon as they could, the Foundation

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:58.140
moved in to increase security around the SCP,
creating Area - 354 and installing a permanent

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.750
security detail.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.629
After this point, the pond started to regularly
spit out a variety of monstrous entities,

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:09.340
almost as if it was reacting to the SCP Foundation's
increased security measures.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.410
After SCP-354-1, the giant bat came SCP-354-2.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:20.190
354-2 was an echidna-like monster the size
of a bear, that was virtually bulletproof

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.100
but unable to escape Area 354.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.660
The foundation neutralized this anomaly with
napalm.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:32.000
SCP-354-3 was a floating black sphere capable
of firing deadly beams of concentrated energy.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.360
The area's head scientist was able to hit
it with a sledgehammer, causing the sphere

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.280
to malfunction and self-destruct before it
was able to escape the area.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.780
The Foundation wasn't as lucky with SCP-354-4.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:49.540
This creature was a reptilian humanoid that
stood roughly 15 feet tall and was unable

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.700
to be put down with gunfire.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.870
This was the first creature from the pond
to successfully escape containment, and was

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:01.050
only able to be neutralized when the Foundation
sent in Mobile Task Force Omega 7, also known

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.139
as “Pandora's Box.”

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:08.550
The data on pond incursions is partially corrupted,
so a complete list of creatures is not available,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.449
but some of the other monsters that came out
of the blood pond included a killer robot,

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:17.319
a set of gigantic tentacles that dragged several
D-class personnel into the pond, a pair of

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:21.740
panther-like creatures - one made of ice and
the other of magma - that ignored foundation

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:27.150
staff and instead fought each other, and one
seemingly normal human man who was executed

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.539
as soon as he emerged from the pond.

00:05:29.539 --> 00:05:34.259
Tests on his body revealed that he was, in
fact, totally normal and would have posed

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:35.350
no threat.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:39.819
These anomalies came out of the pond at fairly
regular intervals for several months, before

00:05:39.819 --> 00:05:43.770
the pond went silent for an unprecedented
22 months.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:47.889
The head scientist at the time noted, “I
suspect this means one of two things.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:51.949
Either the Red Pool has ‘died’ or ‘powered
down’ or whatever the correct term for it

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:55.270
is; or it is ‘charging up’ for something
big to come through.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:00.229
O5 believes the former is the most likely
explanation, and has recalled 30% of our total

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:02.780
personnel and cut 25% of our funding.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:08.020
While I can only hope that they are correct,
if the latter situation is true, we're soon

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:12.669
to face some terrible monstrosity and we won't
have anywhere near the force necessary to

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:13.690
deal with it.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.819
I worry for all of our safety.”

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:21.830
His words would prove eerily prophetic following
the events of Exploratory Mission 354 Alpha.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:25.620
The Foundation's research and development
team built a specialized craft to explore

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.620
the pond.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:30.569
Because of the strange properties of the pond's
density, the craft was essentially made to

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:35.190
be both a submarine, for parts of the pond
where the contents were liquid, and a drill,

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.759
for when the liquid congealed into a semi-solid
towards the bottom.

00:06:38.759 --> 00:06:45.199
The exploration team consisted of Agent Swanson,
Agent Turquoise, Agent 86, Dr. Jay Macarthur,

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:48.990
Chris Simmons, Leroy Tucker, and a pilot named
Marty.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.400
With the team assembled, the ship was sent
down into the pond.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.070
Nothing eventful happened for the first two
days of the mission, but at 4:30 AM on the

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:00.759
third day, gravity suddenly reversed for the
crew of the ship.

00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:04.370
This seemed to indicate that they were approaching
the halfway point, though what would be on

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:07.050
the other side, nobody could say.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:11.289
On the fourth day, the ship surfaced, proving
definitely that the pond was in fact some

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:12.510
sort of portal.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:15.970
The crew looked out of the portholes to see
the darkness of night above them.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:20.050
While sensors outside the ship detected nothing
harmful in the atmosphere around them, the

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:22.470
crew were wary of exiting the craft.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:25.980
The other side of the pond was nothing like
the world the crew knew.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:31.520
For one thing, the night lasted for 28 hours
before dawn came, and when the sun finally

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.729
rose, it was much larger and redder than the
earth's sun.

00:07:35.729 --> 00:07:40.020
Under the light of that strange, red star,
the crew could see that the pond on this side

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.909
was massive compared to where they'd come
in - more like a large lake.

00:07:44.909 --> 00:07:48.680
Surrounding the lake was sand and rocks that
were covered in a kind of moss that disappeared

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.550
under sunlight and regrew during the night.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.379
The team left the ship and started to explore.

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:58.680
During their time in this strange world, they
found that the day lasted just a few hours

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:03.610
shorter than the night, meaning that whatever
planet they were on had roughly a 43-hour-long

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:06.690
rotation as opposed to our own planet's 24.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:10.699
The team found a number of anomalous elements
on their expedition, including razor-sharp

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:14.380
grass that can puncture skin and streams of
liquid carbon dioxide.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:19.270
They heard some loud roars in the distance
once or twice, but other than that the planet

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.591
was eerily silent, with seemingly no animal
life and not even wind.

00:08:23.591 --> 00:08:28.889
When it rained, the soil remained dry, and
based on that, the scientists theorized plants

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:31.680
in this world were more efficient at absorbing
moisture.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:36.580
On the 25th day, the team ran into a huge
metal wall that appeared to be artificially

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.580
constructed.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:42.710
Luckily, Leroy Tucker, a quick-thinking researcher,
was able to rig a blowtorch from camping supplies

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.540
and melt a hole through the metal.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.430
On the other side, there was finally wind,
and odd black grass.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:52.790
That's the extent of what is known about the
other side of the wall, though, because the

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.790
expedition logs are heavily corrupted after
that point, but we know that whatever was

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.390
in there wasn't good, because the team never
returned.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:04.520
Strangely, there's no record of any of the
names mentioned in the ship's log - almost

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:08.520
as if being killed on the other side completely
erased them from history.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.400
No other expeditions into the pond were launched
after that.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.950
On an undisclosed date, a year following the
discovery of the blood pond and construction

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:21.880
of Area 354, the site was completely evacuated,
and the power was cut to the area.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:26.000
Mobile Task Force Theta-12 was dispatched
to investigate the cause of the evacuation,

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.580
but before contact could be established, the
area's on-site nuclear warhead was detonated,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.040
completely destroying the site.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:37.950
MTF Theta 12 was then attacked by a convoy
made up of D-class and other low-ranking staff

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.930
who had evacuated Area 354.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:44.520
It was apparent that there had been some kind
of mutiny within the site, and that a dissolution

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.390
of the chain of command had led to its evacuation
and destruction.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:53.750
The convoy totally annihilated MTF Theta 12,
and no further contact with the former personnel

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.170
of Area-354 has been made since.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:01.600
Following the site's detonation, a new site
was constructed, called simply the Red Pool

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.890
Containment Site.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:07.380
Unlike the previous facility, which focused
on research and neutralization, the new site

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.980
is entirely concerned with containment.

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:14.230
The shift in directive came as a response
to the pond's apparent reactive nature - each

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:18.980
creature that emerged from the pond seemed
to be in retaliation to the Foundation's actions,

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.460
and it was theorized by some that the mutiny
at Area 354 was triggered by some kind of

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.890
psychic attack from the pond itself.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:31.170
An interview in the SCP file on 354 reveals
that there was one more disastrous attempt

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.780
to control and understand the blood pond.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:38.060
According to an interview with a Foundation
agent, the head doctor proposed a scheme to

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:41.620
drain the blood pond using a system of pumps
and hoses.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:46.640
All non-essential personnel were evacuated
in case of emergency, leaving only the pump

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.290
technicians, D-class personnel, and a few
agents for security.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:55.000
However, as soon as the pump was scheduled
to be turned on, everyone at the site experienced

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.120
a mass dissociative episode.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:02.140
The agent described the feeling they all experienced
as like being in a dream and suddenly realizing

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.140
that you're asleep.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.500
He said “Everything stopped being real.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.870
It was like we had to escape right now.”

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:12.390
When asked what happened when the pump was
turned on, he simply explained that it “wouldn't

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:13.390
let them”.

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:17.010
This interview confirmed the theory that the
pond is not only capable of releasing monsters

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:22.920
out into our world, but also that it's capable
of powerful but much more subtle, psychological

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:23.920
attacks.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:29.120
This suggests a chilling possibility - that
the pond isn't just blindly reacting to being

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.460
attacked, but it's fully sentient, and the
actions of the SCP foundation have only served

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.700
to annoy it.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:40.230
And worse, studies of the pond's banks have
provided evidence that the area of congealed

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:44.600
liquid around the perimeter of the pond has
been steadily expanding.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.630
That's right - the pond is getting bigger.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:51.600
The last thing the Foundation agent stationed
at the site said before being dragged out

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:56.860
of the interview and sedated was “It gets
bigger and stronger every day, and now we've

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.450
made it angry!”

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:04.940
Now go check out “SCP - 087 - The Stairwell”
and “SCP - 096 - The Shy Guy” for more

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.459
classic Foundation foes!

